    "description": "M-Lok Adapted Picatinny Rails: Laffs\n\nOriginally had a pack of rails released on Thingiverse years ago; they shadowbanned my work and I forgot to migrate the design to LBRY/Odysee \nbefore repurposing the original drive, losing the data.\n\nRemade the rail design.\n\nRounded edge corners so users don't accidentally jam their hands into hard polymer edges of the rails.\n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 218C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16mm\nWall Thickness: .40mm\nWall Perimeters: 7\nInfill: 50%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 22%\n\n\n\nHardware Needed: \n\n2x M5x10 Hex Screw\n\n2x M-Lok T-Nuts\n",
